Elecraft KX3 Programmer's Reference revision G5 was used as the authoritative
interoperability reference for CAT IF-field semantics. Elecraft names and
commands remain the property of their respective owner. This work adds no new
third-party runtime dependency.

Names including Nexus, KD9TAW, Elecraft, FlexRadio, POTA, SOTA, WWFF, Wavelog,
QRZ, HamQTH, and other vendors, services, or organisations are used only to
identify interoperability targets or external services. No endorsement,
affiliation, sponsorship, or trademark licence is implied.

Android POTA Chase consumes the public Parks on the Air activator-spot API and
worldwide park catalogue from api.pota.app and pota.app. POTA names and park
data remain attributable to Parks on the Air. ShackCQ is an independent
application and does not imply official hunter credit, affiliation, or
authoritative park boundaries.

Android POTA Activate uses the downloaded catalogue and official POTA rules to
prepare local ADIF files. Spotting and log submission are operator-controlled
browser handoffs to pota.app; ShackCQ uses no POTA write API or credentials.

Android Portable Chase consumes the WWFF Spotline public integration spot and
active-agenda JSON feeds from spots.wwff.co and the official downloadable SOTA
summit list from sotadata.org.uk. WWFF and SOTA names and data remain
attributable to their respective programmes. The full WWFF Directory is not
stored without permission. Authorised receive-only SOTA activity is obtained
from the GM4LLD SOTA Cluster at cluster.sota.org.uk:7300 using the operator's
configured DX-cluster login. ShackCQ sends only the login and a bounded history
query, exposes no SOTA posting path, and resolves summit details through the
separately downloaded official summit catalogue. No deprecated private API is used.

